  The original poster probably wants a simple sure-fire strategy for
early wizards.  There doesn't seem to be one that applies strictly to
wizards (See sig.)  Elbereth early and often.  Develop and hide behind
pets.  Stash a lot.  Constantly scrabble for better armor.  Bravely run
away!




  Playing a wizard, especially an early one, means taking advantage of
every trick available.  

  On the one hand, wizards start with 2 spells, 2 rings, a wand, 3
scrolls, and 3 potions.  That generally means there are a number of
tricks to use.  (It's also a great way for a complete newbie to learn
some of the items in the game and their uses.)

  On the other hand, that's a lot of work and rote memorization.  Few
players seem to want to do that.



